  "_commit": {
    "id": "a52849b521bde47ad5ffa6ea9cee1fc50dd9af45",
    "author": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.21.13: lisaClust() regions by position (cell IDs repeated per image); lisa() rows in input order; NA checks; numeric regions in hatchingPlot()\n\n- lisaClust() mapped regions back by cellID, so cell IDs that repeat in each image left most cells without a\n  region. Regions now go back by position; results with unique cell IDs are unchanged (Keren test identical).\n- lisa() returns rows in the order of `cells` (#15), so its curves can be clustered and put straight back on an\n  SCE/SPE; input already ordered by image gives the same matrix. Generated row names follow the input order.\n- lisa()/lisaClust() stop with a message naming the column on missing image IDs, cell types (previously a\n  segfault in the core) or coordinates; unused imageID factor levels are dropped; lisaClust() checks the length\n  of cellWeights; lisa()'s deprecation messages name lisa().\n- hatchingPlot() turns a numeric region column into a factor (#1).\n- tests/testthat/test-inputs.R: regression tests for #1, #12, #14, #15, #16 and the above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013sjhuCgL8kii1snyas2Aj8\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013sjhuCgL8kii1snyas2Aj8\n",
    "time": 1793068607
  },
